  "answer": "The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what `mergeRanges(ranges)` in `ranges.mjs` now does:\n\n**Validation (throws `TypeError`):**\n- Input must be an array.\n- Each element must be an array of exactly two safe integers with `start <= end`.\n\n**Merging logic:**\n- Empty input returns `[]`.\n- Copies each pair into a fresh array (via `.map`) before sorting, so the input array and its pairs are never mutated.\n- Sorts by start, then end.\n- Merges when the next interval overlaps or is adjacent (`range[0] <= last[1] + 1`), which handles touching integers like `[2,4]` + `[5,7]` → `[2,7]`.\n- Contained intervals don't shorten the current interval (only extends `last[1]` when `range[1] > last[1]`).\n- Returns fresh pair arrays inside a fresh result array, sorted by start.\n\n**Verification against the provided tests:**\n- `[[8,10],[1,3],[2,5]]` → `[[1,5],[8,10]]` ✓\n- `[[5,7],[2,4]]` → `[[2,7]]` ✓\n\nThe named export `mergeRanges` is preserved.",
